{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/47848-interesting-ideas-for-splinters","id":47848,"title":"Interesting ideas for Splinters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-12T20:33:32-08:00","id":47848,"title":"Interesting ideas for Splinters","content":"I'm in love with Splinters - the self-contained bubbles of time within a city, caused by Infrastructure, disaster, or cosmic happenstance - and want ideas for some outside of Seattle. I know we're getting the Seed Collection (I wish we knew which cities!) but in the meantime, we have each other. What cities would make for interesting hotbeds of God-Machine activity and would have exciting Splinters? I feel like non-American cities would be best; imagine Rome, with Splinters from the time of the Empire to the modern day and everything inbetween!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T03:34:03-08:00","id":48047,"title":"","content":"I remember Fringe, and suggest a New York where 9/11 didn't happen and the Twin Towers are still up.<br /> For non-American example, I suggest a Berlin where the Wall was never destroyed,<br /> Or a Paris where the Eiffel Tower got dismantled (it originally was very unpopular among artists). For all we know, the God-Machine has some key use for it. It's a huge iron geometric construct, surely there could be many uses for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T09:56:12-08:00","id":48265,"title":"","content":"<ul><li>Chicago where the Chicago Fire didn't happen</li> <li>Hiroshima and/or Nagasaki where Little Boy/Fat Man weren't dropped</li> <li>Roswell where the crash led to something horrendously unplanned-for-by-the-God-Machine (My favorite, I'd add in elements of Delta Green here)</li> <li>Make the Tunguska Blast plot-significant (A Rank 10 Angel Falling?)</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T12:48:33-08:00","id":48412,"title":"","content":"I've writing up setting material for a game set in San Diego (and Tijuana really), and I've been contemplating some kind of alt-history splinter where the whole area is part of Mexico, or ruled by a victorious Japanese Empire. Or maybe the Confederacy...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T12:51:50-08:00","id":48414,"title":"","content":"London where the Normans never invaded.<br /> Rome where the Church never split in two.<br /> Jerusalem where no one ever conquered the Jews.<br /> Victorian London where the God Machine never existed!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T00:55:58-08:00","id":48787,"title":"","content":"San Juan where the attempt English invasion of 1595 was successful.<br /> Hamburg where world war two never happened.<br /> Baghdad that was never sacked by the Mongols.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1544-vectorfox","name":"VectorFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1544_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T20:50:16-08:00","id":55186,"title":"","content":"Any city, any time, where a wealthy local has been building communications posts and letting people use them for free. (cell company that only works in a certain area, but doesn't charge, postal service with a mechanical sorting machine that does it's best to deliver mail even if unstamped, telephone booths where you don't have to pay, telegraph that will send fifty free messages per day)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T12:52:51-08:00","id":55626,"title":"","content":"I'm helping develop a game with a psuedo sci-horror bend that takes place somewhat in the future, with technology advancements and colonies on various planets, and the GM wants to add a faction of Antagonist Aliens. So I pitched a genesis to him, as follows:<br /> <br /> The God Machine, understanding that the Aliens endanger it's great nestegg of Earth, has quelled the Alien Race before they were able to rise up against it and invade our Galaxy. But it hasn't completely succeeded in every causal timeline available, yet, and is reiterating and rebooting the Aliens out of existence in other splinters as the game progresses. Simultaneously giving us a universe where the Aliens have captured Earth and the God Machine struggles to eradicate them, or reboot them out of existence, and a place for the aliens to &quot;fall&quot; into the true causal timeline and go into uprising.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2074-64bitjedi","name":"64bitjedi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}